ps2xIOP: load a module from a buffer reads the bytes from IOP RAM

What it fixes: sceSifLoadModuleBuffer (replaced by the runtime handler,
Kernel/Syscalls/System.cpp:288) ends in IopEmulator::loadModuleBuffer, which read the ELF
through IopHost::readGuest. In the runtime that is the main processor's RAM
(PS2IopHostAdapter::readGuest, ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_iop_host.cpp:132). The game passes an
address in IOP RAM: Battle Stadium D.O.N's loader (0x136670) gets it from
sceSifAllocSysMemory (Stubs/SIF.cpp:309 -> IopMemory::allocate, first address 0x120000), copies
the module there with sceSifSetDma (Stubs/SIF.cpp:629 -> IopSubsystem::writeMemory) and then
loads from that address. The header check therefore ran on unrelated main-memory bytes, every
load returned -1 and the game's retry loop at 0x136708 never ended.

The change: IopEmulator reads the ELF from its own RAM first (new
IopModuleLoader::readElfFromIopMemory, sharing the parsing with readElfFromGuest through one
template) and falls back to the host's main memory only when no valid ELF is there, which keeps
the behaviour the emulator's own tests rely on (loadModuleBuffer(0x100) with the image staged in
the host's memory). No path makes a load succeed without a valid ELF.

How it was verified: tests/runtime/module_buffer_load_test.cpp builds a relocatable IRX in
memory, puts it in IOP RAM at the address allocateMemory returns (0x120000), calls
IopSubsystem::loadModuleBuffer and checks the module id is above zero and that the start function
ran. Without this patch: moduleId=-1 and the test fails; with it: moduleId=1 and it passes. The
same test checks the main-memory fallback and that a non-ELF buffer is still refused. Not covered:
the runtime adapter and the SDK handlers (they need the whole runtime library). Applies on top of
patches 0001-0003 and together with 0006.

Original work for this project, against PS2Recomp commit 2c5fbb9389e11dd95693385969490c9e8e6f57b4
(GPL-3.0).

diff --git a/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/iop_emulator.cpp b/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/iop_emulator.cpp
index e5f63a9..00ed753 100644
--- a/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/iop_emulator.cpp
+++ b/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/iop_emulator.cpp
@@ -655,7 +655,11 @@ namespace ps2x::iop::detail
         ModuleLoadResult loadModuleBuffer(uint32_t guestAddress, const void *arguments, uint32_t argumentSize)
         {
             std::vector<uint8_t> image;
-            if (!IopModuleLoader::readElfFromGuest(host, guestAddress, image))
+            // The SDK function takes an address in IOP RAM (the game copies the module there with
+            // sceSifSetDma). Read it from the emulator's own RAM first; fall back to the host's
+            // main memory for hosts that hand over a main-memory address.
+            if (!IopModuleLoader::readElfFromIopMemory(memory, guestAddress, image) &&
+                !IopModuleLoader::readElfFromGuest(host, guestAddress, image))
                 return {true, -1, -1};
             std::ostringstream tag;
             tag << "buffer@0x" << std::hex << guestAddress;
diff --git a/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/services/iop_module_loader.cpp b/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/services/iop_module_loader.cpp
index 80e59d6..3166e2b 100644
--- a/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/services/iop_module_loader.cpp
+++ b/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/services/iop_module_loader.cpp
@@ -320,10 +320,11 @@ namespace ps2x::iop::detail
         return ok;
     }
 
-    bool IopModuleLoader::readElfFromGuest(IopHost &host, uint32_t guestAddress, std::vector<uint8_t> &bytes)
+    template <typename Reader>
+    static bool readElfImage(const Reader &readBytes, uint32_t guestAddress, std::vector<uint8_t> &bytes)
     {
         Elf32Ehdr header{};
-        if (!host.readGuest(guestAddress, &header, sizeof(header)) || !validElfHeader(header))
+        if (!readBytes(guestAddress, &header, sizeof(header)) || !validElfHeader(header))
             return false;
 
         uint64_t required = sizeof(header);
@@ -334,7 +335,7 @@ namespace ps2x::iop::detail
             return false; // Should we log an error here? TODO check later
 
         bytes.resize(static_cast<size_t>(required));
-        if (!host.readGuest(guestAddress, bytes.data(), bytes.size()))
+        if (!readBytes(guestAddress, bytes.data(), bytes.size()))
             return false;
 
         if (header.shnum != 0u && header.shentsize >= sizeof(Elf32Shdr))
@@ -364,7 +365,21 @@ namespace ps2x::iop::detail
             return false;
 
         bytes.resize(static_cast<size_t>(required));
-        return host.readGuest(guestAddress, bytes.data(), bytes.size());
+        return readBytes(guestAddress, bytes.data(), bytes.size());
+    }
+
+    bool IopModuleLoader::readElfFromGuest(IopHost &host, uint32_t guestAddress, std::vector<uint8_t> &bytes)
+    {
+        return readElfImage([&host](uint32_t address, void *destination, size_t size)
+                            { return host.readGuest(address, destination, size); },
+                            guestAddress, bytes);
+    }
+
+    bool IopModuleLoader::readElfFromIopMemory(const IopMemory &memory, uint32_t iopAddress, std::vector<uint8_t> &bytes)
+    {
+        return readElfImage([&memory](uint32_t address, void *destination, size_t size)
+                            { return memory.readRam(address, destination, size); },
+                            iopAddress, bytes);
     }
 
     IopImageLoadResult IopModuleLoader::load(std::span<const uint8_t> image, IopMemory &memory, uint32_t moduleCursor)
diff --git a/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/services/iop_module_loader.h b/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/services/iop_module_loader.h
index 6cd9ef6..a35db16 100644
--- a/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/services/iop_module_loader.h
+++ b/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/services/iop_module_loader.h
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@ namespace ps2x::iop::detail
     public:
         [[nodiscard]] static bool readWholeHostFile(IopHost &host, std::string_view guestPath, std::vector<uint8_t> &bytes);
         [[nodiscard]] static bool readElfFromGuest(IopHost &host, uint32_t guestAddress, std::vector<uint8_t> &bytes);
+        [[nodiscard]] static bool readElfFromIopMemory(const IopMemory &memory, uint32_t iopAddress, std::vector<uint8_t> &bytes);
         [[nodiscard]] static IopImageLoadResult load(std::span<const uint8_t> image, IopMemory &memory, uint32_t moduleCursor);
     };
